      "code": "EML146",
      "message": "Column \"Post.status\" has no %%field enum binding.",
      "line": 23,
      "hint": "Declare  %%enum PostStatus: ...  and bind it with  %%field Post.status enum: PostStatus. Unbound, the Application Dictionary records free text and the form accepts values the state machine cannot act on.",
      "autoFixable": false
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "code": "EML149",
      "message": "\"PostTag\" looks like a line item of \"Post\" but declares no parent.",
      "line": 41,
      "hint": "If a list of every PostTag away from its Post is not a screen anyone opens, declare `%%entity PostTag parent: Post` — the dictionary then drops its dashboard card and gives it a tab inside the Post window, linked on post_id. If it is a thing in its own right, leave it: a reference is the opposite on all three questions (§3.5.1).",
      "autoFixable": false
    },
    {
